# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to .env.local for local development. In production these are set as
# Vercel Environment Variables (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables).
# All three are SERVER-side only — none is NEXT_PUBLIC_, so none is exposed in
# the browser bundle.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the self-hosted n8n instance (Oracle Cloud). No trailing slash.
# The webhook path is appended per region by app/api/audit/route.ts.
#   IND -> $N8N_BASE_URL/webhook/audit-field-photov2
#   US  -> $N8N_BASE_URL/webhook/audit-field-photo-us
N8N_BASE_URL=https://n8n.kratuailabs.com

# Which code regions this deployment may serve. Comma-separated.
#
#   IND      India customer    — US surface is neither rendered nor callable
#   US       US customer       — India surface is neither rendered nor callable
#   IND,US   internal / demo   — region switch visible
#
# This is the access boundary between customers. app/api/audit/route.ts
# rejects any region outside this list with HTTP 403, so it holds even against
# a hand-crafted request. UNSET FAILS CLOSED TO 'IND'.
ENABLED_REGIONS=IND

# Vercel Blob token for /api/upload. Provisioned automatically when a Blob
# store is linked to the project; set it explicitly only for local dev.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# Optional. How long the proxy waits on n8n before returning HTTP 504.
# Defaults to 240000 (240s). Keep it under the plan's function limit:
# Vercel Hobby caps functions at 60s, Pro at 300s.
# AUDIT_TIMEOUT_MS=240000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audit Records (app/api/history/route.ts)
#
# Shared secret for the n8n audit-history webhook. Must equal the VALUE of the
# httpHeaderAuth credential bound to that webhook, whose header name must be
# x-audit-history-key.
#
# Records are OFF until this is set: the API returns 503 RECORDS_NOT_CONFIGURED
# and the UI hides the tab. That keeps a data-retrieval endpoint over customer
# sites and their fire-safety deficiencies from existing by accident.
#
# Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HISTORY_API_KEY=

# Optional. Records queries are indexed lookups, so this is deliberately much
# shorter than the audit timeout. Defaults to 30000 (30s).
# HISTORY_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access control (middleware.ts)
#
# HTTP Basic auth over the page AND the API routes. Every audit is a paid vision
# call, so an open URL is a metered spend endpoint — and you cannot hand an open
# URL to a customer.
#
# BOTH must be set for protection to apply. With either missing the middleware
# is inert, which is why deploying it cannot lock you out. Set them per
# deployment so each customer has its own credential.
#
# Generate a password you will have to TYPE into a browser prompt. Prefer hex
# over base64: `openssl rand -base64 32` emits + / and = , which are easy to
# mistype and easy to lose from the end of a copy-paste.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 24
#
# Surrounding whitespace is trimmed from both values, so a stray trailing
# newline from a pasted value will not lock you out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUDIT_ACCESS_USER=
# AUDIT_ACCESS_PASSWORD=
